In a medium #saucepan{} over medium heat, heat @olive oil{1%teaspoon}. Add minced @garlic{2%cloves}(minced) and @fresh ginger{1/2%teaspoon}(minced). Cook for ~{1%minute} until fragrant.

Pour @low-sodium vegetable broth{2%cups} and @low-sodium soy sauce{2%teaspoons} into the #saucepan{}. Bring to a boil. Add @ramen noodles{1%ounces}(seasoning packet discarded) and cook for ~{3%minutes} until tender.

Stir in @fresh spinach{1%cup} and cook for ~{1%minute} until wilted.

Reduce heat to a gentle simmer. Crack @large eggs{2} into the broth, spacing them apart. Poach eggs for ~{3%minutes} until whites are set but yolks are still runny.

Divide noodles and broth between two #bowls{}. Top each with a poached egg. Serve immediately, garnished with chopped @scallions{}(Chopped).
